== Background <sec:background>

Fire detection systems have traditionally relied on single-sensor technologies, which are often prone to false alarms in complex indoor environments. This thesis explores the development of an *Autonomous Sensing Node*—a specialized edge intelligence unit designed to distinguish between real fire events and common false alarm triggers using sensor fusion and TinyML.

The system leverages the Arduino UNO R4 WiFi architecture, where the Renesas RA4M1 microcontroller serves as the primary "inference brain," while the ESP32-S3 manages telemetry and location-based tagging.
